    "publishedfileid" "3799989713"
    "contentfolder" "${CONTENT_PATH}"
    "previewfile" "${PREVIEW_IMG}"
    "visibility" "2"
    "title" "Predictable Belt Filters"
    "description" "[h1]Predictable Belt Filters[/h1]
The base game has a bug where Belt filters will not correctly show their output shape in the shape preview.
This cause all downstream simulations and predictions to stop working!

Well, after seeing many threads go by on reddit and discord about this problem, I decided to fix the problem!

[h2]What this changes[/h2]
[list]
[*]Filter a shape: the forward belt predicts only that shape, the side belt predicts the rest.
[*]Filter 'on': everything forward, nothing to the side.
[*]Filter 'off': nothing forward, everything to the side.
[*]Nothing wired: Shows all shapes on every side.
[/list]

[h2]Dependencies[/h2]
[list]
[*]Requires Shapez Shifter.
[/list]

Bugs and requests: https://github.com/QuinnBast/Shapez2-Mods/issues
Licensed under Apache 2.0."
}
